-- A ten-slot product scene of 25-value objects (Nil | Obj shape color),
-- read by one neural network, counting the red objects. The Scene domain is
-- 25^10 values: scalar compiles it in 0.1 s, and the batched backend used to
-- run out of memory listing that domain for the dense-mode DOMAIN constant
-- (task batched-compile-ooms-on-wide-product-scene; the scalar-side wall was
-- task enum-tag-accessor-walks-product-domain). Being in the corpus at all is
-- half the test: the batched-eligibility probe compiles every corpus program
-- while the test tree is built. Same logits as
-- TestInternals.wideProductSceneAccessorCompilesFast; the count is
-- Poisson-binomial in pObj_i * pRed_i. Only the tail counts are queried: a
-- middle count costs ~C(10,k) on the scalar engine (task
-- scene-count-query-binomial-in-count), seconds per row.
-- No `batched` token: the batched compile is checked (the eligibility probe
-- compiles every corpus program, and Internals'
-- wideProductSceneBatchedCompilesFast pins it), but running the emitted
-- kernel nests one split loop per slot and did not finish in 20 minutes at
-- ten slots; that runtime is task batched-count-chain-enumeration-factorial,
-- which should add the token when it lands.
backends: interpreter, julia, python
